  (a) Oxygen #h(2em) (b) Nitrogen #h(2em) (c) Carbon dioxide #h(2em) (d) Hydrogen

+ Where does most photosynthesis occur in a plant?
  (a) Roots #h(2em) (b) Stem #h(2em) (c) Flowers #h(2em) (d) Leaves

+ What is the role of chlorophyll?
  (a) It absorbs light energy. #h(1em) (b) It carries water to the leaves.
  (c) It stores sugar. #h(2em) (d) It opens and closes stomata.

+ Which of these is the correct word equation for photosynthesis?
  (a) Oxygen + glucose → carbon dioxide + water
  (b) Carbon dioxide + water → glucose + oxygen
  (c) Glucose + water → carbon dioxide + oxygen
  (d) Water + oxygen → glucose + carbon dioxide

